#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""jess-coder: a sandboxed Qwen Code box on Jupiter, driven by Jess's brain.

  jess-coder [start] <name> [--continue] [--ask] [--hours H] [--task TEXT]
      Open (or resume) session <name>: a fresh, offline container on coder-net
      with Qwen Code in auto-approve mode (--ask: confirm each action). The
      workspace persists in /srv/jess-coder/sessions/<name>; --continue also
      resumes the last conversation. --task runs one instruction headless
      (no terminal UI) and exits; the changes stay in the workspace.
  jess-coder patch <name> [--allow PATH]... [--show]
      Get the session's changes as a checked patch file, ready for `git apply`
      in a worktree. Files that would run on this host before you review them
      (CI, Claude Code config, scripts, compose, ...) are refused unless allowed.
  jess-coder ls                     sessions, running boxes, live tokens
  jess-coder rm <name> [-y]         delete a session's workspace
  jess-coder selftest               run the box isolation self-test
  jess-coder build [--if-stale]     build the box image (docker compose)
  jess-coder enabled                exit 0 if CODER_ENABLED is on in .env

Docs + threat model: docs/CODER.md. Stdlib only. Install with
  ln -s ~/gateway_nerves/scripts/jess-coder ~/.local/bin/jess-coder

What this script guarantees (the box itself is the boundary; docs/CODER.md):
* every box is a new `docker run --rm` with the flags in box_command(): read-only
  root, no capabilities, no-new-privileges, its own uid, resource limits, no
  logs, and either coder-net (sessions, self-test) or no network at all (patch,
  rm);
* before a box opens, coder-net is checked (internal, isolated gateway, no
  IPv6, no foreign members) and the box runs the isolation self-test, which
  must pass;
* the coder token is minted per session, reaches the box only through the
  environment (never argv), and is revoked when the session ends; the box
  ends itself at the token's expiry (and the launcher kills it then too);
* this script never runs git inside a box's folder, and never trusts a box's
  diff: it applies it to a clean clone of the base and keeps only what git
  regenerates there (cmd_patch).
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import codecs
